diff a/src/Daoris.Desktop/README.md b/src/Daoris.Desktop/README.md	(rejected hunks)
@@ -920 +920 @@ stand does no work; the others name what no version tells (`Untold`) and work at
-| `help` | Ask Daoris's conversation in its room (`START_HELP`, the one running or starting, or a new one answered `starting` once its record is open, its room read and its agent spawned after with the words said meanwhile held as its queue, HELPSTART1; the reading waited for 30 s, past which the room as last written serves and the conversation says so, HELPSTUCK1). `START_HELP` and `HELP_START_FROM` take the `workspace` the window is on (ASKSCOPE1a, D158's ASKSCOPE1 note): read at the press, kept by the record, choosing its account, and named in every answer; none is `default`'s, as before, and one this machine does not hold is refused. One runs, and one starts (`HelpStarting`), per workspace; one the person finished is never carried on, waited for up to 5 s, then answered `finishing` (HELPNEWCHAT1); setting one aside for a start-from or a going-on takes its own workspace's alone; its tools default to its workspace and read or propose into another by naming it, or `all` (D253). Each runs in its workspace's own room (ASKSCOPE1b, D158's ASKSCOPE1b note): `default`'s is `help`, the whole machine as before, and a named workspace's a folder of its own beside it (`help-<name>`), written from the facts projected to that workspace before any count or limit, its first lines saying what is the workspace's and what the machine's; one started in `help` before goes on there, and the facts' catch-up writes each room again from its own workspace's facts. Then its proposals with the person's Apply or Not now (`HELP_PROPOSALS`, told by event since NOBLOCK1, `HELP_APPLY`, `HELP_DISMISS`; a go's dismiss settles its card and tells the conversation nothing, ASKDISMISS1), each kind judged and applied by the driver's class for it under `Help/Proposals/` (a workflow's whole version and its choice by `HelpWorkflowProposals`, WORKFLOW1h-b; since FLOWCHART2e a change to the open draft, judged against the drafts the conversation's record was told, its card carrying `draft`, `changes`, `problems` and `proposed`, and `HELP_APPLY`'s `taken` and `left` naming each change the editor took or left, which settles it; without them its Apply opens the place's Workflow and stands, saving and choosing nothing); its history, kept on this machine only (ASKHIST1): every conversation ordered and searched, then answered a page at a time (`HELP_CONVERSATIONS` {q, offset, limit} answers `{conversations, cut, total, next}`, ASKHIST1d1, D158; `help list --offset --limit` is its terminal door), one workspace's or every one's (`workspace`, ASKSCOPE1d: that workspace's kept before anything is ordered, searched or counted, none naming every one's; each row's `workspace`, after `mode`, the one it started in, `default` for a record from before; `help list --workspace <name> | --all`, the latter labelling each row), named and pinned (`HELP_RENAME`, `HELP_PIN`), and a new conversation started from an earlier one's words (`HELP_START_FROM`). Its focus (ASKSCOPE2b, D253 point 3's note) is what it is about, kept on its `sessions/<id>.help.json` beside its name and pin as `focus`, `focusNext` and `foci`, each a place `{kind: machine \| workspace \| repository, workspace?, repository?}` (`HelpFocus`, the page's `help/focus.ts`): `HELP_FOCUS` {session, focus} answers `{session, focus, focusNext}`, before any words setting its first focus and after them the one its next words take, the applied one chosen again clearing what waited, or `{session, refused, said}` for `unknown-place`, `not-help` or `ended`; `ask-daoris focus <id> machine \| <workspace> \| <workspace>/<repository>` is its terminal door. A record from before reads its home's (`default`'s as this machine). `START_HELP` takes `focus` for the one it places and answers each one's, `HELP_START_FROM`'s takes the earlier one's applied focus, and `HELP_CONVERSATIONS` takes `about` (never beside `workspace`: its home there or inside it, or a focus held there; `help list --about <place>`), each row answering `focus` and `focusNext` after `workspace`. Going on in one is `SESSION_INPUT`'s, and deleting one `SESSION_DELETE`'s. Its access mode (HELPMODE1a1, D183) is the driver's `helpMode`, restricted until the person names full, read at each start, a conversation going on among them: full runs its harness's own mode that asks nothing (`ChatAgent.FullPosture`), refused plainly on a harness with none or one whose agent does not offer it, and hands every plugin server; `daoris ask-daoris mode [restricted\|full]` is its terminal door, and `SET_HELP_MODE` {mode} its route over the same key (HELPMODE1a2), the state answering it as `helpMode`, its page HELPMODE1b's. The mode a start got, the effective one, is its record's (`helpMode`, machine-local), told at the open; a conversation going on under another records the new one and its transcript's first line says the change; each history row names it (`mode`, after `live`). A switch never reaches a conversation as it runs, on either door: its rules, servers and room were handed for its start's mode, so the switch takes its next start, and a running one under another mode is told so on its console (D183's HELPMODE1a2 note). What each start handed is kept as a receipt (HELPWIRED1, D183 point 4), written once its inputs are composed and before its agent starts, from the spawn itself: its mode, agent, version, account, folder, door and posture, the rules as its settings file holds them, Daoris's own tools (none in full access), the skills, each server handed, handed by full access without an approval, or withheld with why (a browser with no host among them), the checkouts it may read, and in restricted mode what it lacks with each door; never a server's command, arguments or environment, nor the spawn's. A going-on adds one and keeps the earlier, in `sessions/<id>.wired.json`, which a delete takes; `HELP_WIRED` {session} answers `{session, recorded, receipts}`, the newest first, `recorded: false` for a conversation from before. `HELP_PUBLISHED` {session} (ASKQUESTS1) answers `{session, published}`: what the conversation's Applies published, the newest first, each `{at, proposal, kind, workspace, ask, quest}` with an id the service's answer did not name left out, kept in `<home>/data/sessions/<id>.published.json` beside its other files; a read, its key under `help`, and the page reads each one's state from the pushed quests, asks and sessions. What an Apply did, and a proposal refused before it was shown, are said into the conversation as Daoris's word (`ChatRunner.Tell`, `from: daoris`), a turn the record keeps as Daoris's; a change's Not now stays the person's. A receipt keeps the `housekeeping` its start was handed (HELPMODE1c2a): the operations the home's `configured-access.json` chose then, whose connector tools its allow-list names and its room says. Each housekeeping tool's call reaches no route: it is a keyed `housekeep` request in the home's session requests, taken by the loop running the conversation, judged by `HelpHousekeeping` (the record Ask Daoris's, the operation chosen now and handed at this start, the repository its workspace's with a checkout here) and answered beside it, the cleanup's own judges called for the act. Each chosen setting's tool (HELPMODE1c3) is a keyed `set` request the same way, judged by `HelpSettings` (the same checks, then the `setting` proposal's own) and applied with no Apply through the driver file's writer, `DriverConfig.ResolvePath(home)` loaded, edited and saved under its lock; each answer is kept as a `help.setting` line in the machine log. Its read of a checkout (HELPMODE1c4, `checkout_read`, for every agent, in place of restricted mode's `Read` and git rules on the checkouts) is a keyed `read` request the same way, judged by `HelpCheckouts` (the record Ask Daoris's, the repository its workspace's with a checkout here, readable under D107, not turned off now and handed at this start, its receipt's `checkouts`; the path walked a name at a time inside the checkout, no `..`, root, drive, stream, pattern, git's own folder or link leading out, and `git check-ignore` asked of it and each folder on its way, a read git cannot judge refused) and answered with what was read as `text`: a file's text cut at 200 KB between characters, a folder's entries, or `git status` and `git branch --list` |
